1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Hello everyone, in the 2026.0 version, when applying hair loss or hair material, it can maintain the effect of the gap line and the sticker can be seen.

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,000
In the past, these details were often blocked by hair.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,000
This update ensures that the craft structure is still visible and the sticker can be perfectly displayed on the surface of the hair,

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:28,000
thereby improving the visual quality and authenticity of hair-dyeing clothing, hair-dyeing toys, and home-made fabric.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Let's take a look at how it works.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:39,000
When you use the editor's sewing line tool to select a fabric type and set it as a single or multiple sewing lines of a hair-dyeing or hair-dyeing only dyeing clothing,

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,000
a new hair-dyeing reduction option will appear in the property editor.

8
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:48,000
In this thickness section, you can adjust the width from 0 mm to 100 mm.

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,000
The unit will be set based on the unit of the user, which is used to adjust the area where the hair will be removed.

10
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The higher the value, the larger the hair-free area.

11
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
In this example, I will set this value to 2 mm.

12
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:07,000
By using the gradient setting under the neckline, you can adjust the distance between the hair-dyeing area and the hair-dyeing area to a range of 0 to 100.

13
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Since the material type of this fabric is hair-dyeing, the result will be visible immediately in the 3D window,

14
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:18,000
but you can also check the final result in the rendering window to get a higher sense of reality.

15
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,000
In the previous CLO version, the sticker will be applied to hair-dyeing or hair-dyeing materials.

16
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Usually, it will cause the hair to overlap and block the sticker, making it invisible in the rendering window.

17
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:34,000
For example, after applying the hair-dyeing material, although the 2D window shows a embroidery sticker,

18
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,000
it will not appear in the 3D window.

19
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:40,000
If it is a hair-dyeing material, it is also invisible in the 3D window.

20
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,000
In the new version, if you use the adjustment sticker tool to select the sticker,

21
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:48,000
you will notice that the hair-dyeing reduction option has been added to the property editor.

22
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,000
When the sticker is applied to the hair-dyeing clothing, this option will be defaulted.

23
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:52,000
You can click on the button.

24
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Here, you can activate or stop this option by clicking on the box.

25
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,000
When the hair-dyeing is used, it seems that the hair-dyeing has been trimmed in the sticker area,

26
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:05,000
so that the sticker is completely visible in the 3D window and rendering window.

27
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Please note that according to the shape and parameters of the hair,

28
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,000
such as length and curve, the hair-dyeing may still cover the sticker in some areas.

29
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Please note this when using long hair-dyeing or long hair-dyeing materials.

30
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
If necessary, please consider adjusting the parameters.

31
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:29,000
In addition, if your pattern has non-transparent information, the hair will be visible in transparent areas.

32
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:35,000
For example, this sticker center is completely transparent, so the hair will be visible in the specific area.

33
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:42,000
With the introduction of this function in the 2026.0 version, you can better control the design of hair-dyeing materials.

34
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Whether it is a clothing accessory, a hair-dyeing toy, or a home-made imitation,

35
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:50,000
while maintaining the seam line and the sticker are perfectly visible on the surface of the hair,

36
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,000
you can completely control the length and change of the hair,

37
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,000
thereby improving the quality and accuracy of the design.

38
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:04,000
In the 2026.0 version, in addition to displaying or hiding specific measurement values,

39
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:08,000
it also increases the possibility of displaying measurement points in the style picture rendering.

40
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,000
The goal is to obtain more technical and information-based style picture rendering,

41
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,000
and accurately display the measurement value of the clothing.

42
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Let's take a look at it through an example.

43
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Some measurement points have already been added to this file,

44
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,000
which are used to determine the measurement size and position of the clothing.

45
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:26,000
After the fire style picture is rendered, the line contains the 2D measurement size option.

46
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:31,000
By clicking the eye icon, you can switch the display or hide of the 2D measurement size.

47
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:35,000
You will notice that the measurement size of the corresponding measurement point will be displayed with it.

48
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:39,000
If necessary, you can change the line color and its opacity.

49
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:43,000
This option will apply to the visualization of all measurement points in the project.

50
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:47,000
However, if you need to hide any of them, you can use the measurement point table.

51
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:50,000
You can find the same eye icon next to each measurement point.

52
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:56,000
All you have to do is click the measurement point you want to hide to get a clearer and more reasonable style picture rendering.

53
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:03,000
By using the 2026.0 version, your style picture rendering is more accurate and reasonable than ever before.

54
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Now let's start to completely control your measurement point visibility and simplify your technical package.

55
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,000
In the previous CLO version, when the rendering has a reflective material,

56
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,000
for example, the image of metal and glass,

57
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:23,000
the use of the ground shadow option will lead to the environment of the ground shadow appearing in the reflection of the object.

58
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:28,000
In the 2026.0 version, you can now remove these shadows from the reflection,

59
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:30,000
while still maintaining the shadow on the ground,

60
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:33,000
allowing us to see an improvement in this image.

61
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:36,000
As you can see, this virtual model is made of glass,

62
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:40,000
and has a mirroring effect that forms a reflective light on a layer of metal.

63
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:44,000
In addition, the attached metal material on the case will also reflect light.

64
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:46,000
In the light attribute of the window rendering,

65
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:50,000
the use of the ground shadow option will apply the shadow on the floor.

66
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:54,000
However, because this shadow has a reflection of the environment on the surface,

67
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:58,000
this will lead to the image being visible in the reflection of the virtual model and the object.

68
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,000
From the beginning of this version,

69
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:03,000
the bottom of the ground shadow added a non-reflective option.

70
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:06,000
When you activate this option by selecting the frame,

71
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:09,000
you need to press the synchronize rendering button to apply this change.

72
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:12,000
You will notice that the environment of the ground shadow is no longer in the glass and metal material,

73
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:15,000
and the reflection is no longer in the glass and metal material.

74
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Now, by using the new function of Claw2026.0,

75
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:21,000
which does not participate in the reflection of the ground shadow,

76
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,000
you can achieve a surprising and clear reflection,

77
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,000
and no needless shadows,

78
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:28,000
and thus further enhance your rendering experience.

